\code{\link[=target_threshold]{target_threshold()}}, \code{\link[=target_coverage]{target_coverage()}} or
\code{\link[=target_metric]{target_metric()}}.
\item \code{\link[=selective_fit]{selective_fit()}} learns the threshold on a calibration set and returns a
selector. \code{predict()} applies it to new data: a row is accepted when
its score is less than or equal to the threshold, otherwise the
prediction is withheld (abstain).
\item \code{\link[=selective_curve]{selective_curve()}} and \code{\link[=aurc]{aurc()}} evaluate the risk-coverage trade-off.
}
